WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:06.580
In managed hosting, select an available strategy and market in your account strategy slots.

2
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.100
Wait for installation to finish before creating an agent.

3
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:15.120
For source software, follow the plugin instructions shipped with your exact release.

4
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.060
A standalone add-on requires a compatible dashboard edition.

5
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.040
Open Agents and look for the installed strategy in the creation choices.

6
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:33.060
If none appears, check that you saved the slot for this workspace and that installation completed.

7
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.860
Refresh after completion.

8
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.380
Buying or selecting a strategy does not by itself prove it was installed successfully.

9
00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:48.280
Create an agent using an installed strategy and a supported market.

10
00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.440
Use a descriptive name so you can identify it later.

11
00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.360
Read the confirmation and initial state.

12
00:00:55.160 --> 00:01:03.260
The hosted creation workflow starts the agent and its associated farm paused, with no allocation, so configuration can be reviewed first.

13
00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:11.840
Set the trading budget only after confirming the account balance and existing exposure.

14
00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:17.360
Increasing allocation does not deposit funds, and decreasing it does not withdraw them.

15
00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:21.920
Do not double count funds already committed to other agents or open positions.

16
00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:25.440
Keep the agent paused while changing its allocation.

17
00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:34.620
Review the risk controls exposed by your edition, including position size and drawdown settings.

18
00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:38.680
Read the units: a percentage is different from a dollar amount.

19
00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.500
Understand whether a limit blocks new entries, cancels orders or requests an exit.

20
00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:47.500
Do not assume every stop control does all three.

21
00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:58.200
Before starting, confirm the network, installed strategy, market data, approved key and available allocation.

22
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.820
Use test funds to validate the workflow.

23
00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.120
After starting, inspect the latest decision.

24
00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:06.540
Capital is not an entry signal.

25
00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:11.320
If the strategy waits, read why instead of raising risk to force a trade.
